meaning:
Many online scams are often associated with the Advance-fee scam. This scam and other types of fraud are often referred to as “419”. The number “419” refers to the section of the Nigerian Criminal Code dealing with fraud, the charges and penalties for offenders.

Many scammers may come from African countries such as Nigeria (Naija) or Ghana.

@JuniorBullet

The main reason as to why this scam is done, is because the service fees to transfer large sums of money between people/accounts are often too high (up to a third is some cases). By using other people’s accounts to pass money through can save the scammer money.

KMT stands for “Kiss(ing) my teeth”, which is a typical reaction for something that annoys someone.

